1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,365
It is festival week, and the Chai
Corner queue reaches the road.

2
00:00:04,665 --> 00:00:06,566
Everyone is working flat out.

3
00:00:07,116 --> 00:00:09,495
Asha makes chai as fast as she can.

4
00:00:09,495 --> 00:00:11,423
Cups pile up, and go cold.

5
00:00:11,723 --> 00:00:13,776
Kabir is stuck counting change.

6
00:00:13,776 --> 00:00:15,331
The line stops moving.

7
00:00:15,631 --> 00:00:17,928
The helpers run out of clean cups.

8
00:00:17,928 --> 00:00:20,313
Everyone is busy, but nothing fits.

9
00:00:20,963 --> 00:00:22,572
Hard work is not enough.

10
00:00:22,572 --> 00:00:24,467
The work has to fit together.

11
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:28,010
Ravi, the owner, has
two jobs to do at once.

12
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:29,864
The first is directing.

13
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:34,230
Guiding people while they work, by
telling, helping and encouraging them.

14
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,397
The second is coordinating.

15
00:00:36,397 --> 00:00:39,943
Making everyone's work fit
together, at the right time.

16
00:00:40,293 --> 00:00:41,928
Directing moves people.

17
00:00:41,928 --> 00:00:44,744
Coordinating makes them move as one team.

18
00:00:45,394 --> 00:00:47,227
Directing has four parts.

19
00:00:47,577 --> 00:00:48,477
Supervision.

20
00:00:48,469 --> 00:00:51,387
Watching the work, and
helping on the spot.

21
00:00:51,737 --> 00:00:52,751
Communication.

22
00:00:52,751 --> 00:00:55,691
Clear words, so everyone knows what to do.

23
00:00:56,041 --> 00:00:56,941
Leadership.

24
00:00:56,815 --> 00:00:59,351
Showing the way, and setting the example.

25
00:00:59,701 --> 00:01:00,601
Motivation.

26
00:01:00,591 --> 00:01:03,416
Giving people a reason to do their best.

27
00:01:04,066 --> 00:01:06,036
Now watch coordination at work.

28
00:01:06,036 --> 00:01:07,912
First, the rush without it.

29
00:01:08,262 --> 00:01:09,705
Asha brews nonstop.

30
00:01:09,705 --> 00:01:11,807
Kabir takes cash one by one.

31
00:01:11,807 --> 00:01:13,690
Cups wait, and go cold.

32
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:17,025
In ten minutes, the queue
grows to eighteen people.

33
00:01:17,675 --> 00:01:20,741
Next day, Ravi gathers
the team before opening.

34
00:01:20,741 --> 00:01:22,774
Pay first, and take a token.

35
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:25,073
Kabir calls out the tokens.

36
00:01:25,073 --> 00:01:27,442
Asha brews exactly that many cups.

37
00:01:27,792 --> 00:01:29,626
Now the queue keeps moving.

38
00:01:29,626 --> 00:01:32,502
No cold cups, and only
four people waiting.

39
00:01:33,152 --> 00:01:36,119
An American thinker
explained why this works.

40
00:01:36,469 --> 00:01:41,012
Mary Parker Follett wrote about how
people work together, back in the nineteen

41
00:01:41,012 --> 00:01:41,912
twenties.

42
00:01:42,076 --> 00:01:47,999
In a lecture published in 1937, she
gave four principles of coordination.

43
00:01:48,349 --> 00:01:49,352
Direct contact.

44
00:01:49,352 --> 00:01:52,532
People who share the work
talk to each other directly.

45
00:01:52,882 --> 00:01:53,905
Early stages.

46
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:57,818
Coordinate while plans are
made, not after things go wrong.

47
00:01:58,168 --> 00:01:59,526
Reciprocal relating.

48
00:01:59,526 --> 00:02:01,913
Every part affects every other part.

49
00:02:02,263 --> 00:02:04,158
And a continuous process.

50
00:02:04,158 --> 00:02:05,988
Coordination never stops.

51
00:02:06,638 --> 00:02:09,115
So what does this look like at work today?

52
00:02:09,465 --> 00:02:10,448
Supervision.

53
00:02:10,448 --> 00:02:14,596
A site supervisor checks everyone's
safety gear every morning.

54
00:02:14,946 --> 00:02:15,993
Communication.

55
00:02:15,993 --> 00:02:20,044
Nurses hand over each patient's
notes at the change of shift.

56
00:02:20,394 --> 00:02:21,294
Leadership.

57
00:02:21,199 --> 00:02:24,951
On the busiest day, the store
manager works the counter too.

58
00:02:25,301 --> 00:02:26,201
Motivation.

59
00:02:26,171 --> 00:02:30,018
A company praises its best
performers in front of everyone.

60
00:02:30,368 --> 00:02:31,320
Coordination.

61
00:02:31,320 --> 00:02:36,063
Before a plane flies again, the cleaning,
fuel and baggage teams all finish

62
00:02:36,063 --> 00:02:36,963
on time.

63
00:02:37,477 --> 00:02:40,440
But can directing and
coordinating go wrong?

64
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:41,340
Yes.

65
00:02:41,317 --> 00:02:42,376
The good side.

66
00:02:42,376 --> 00:02:45,405
Faster service, less
waste, and a calmer team.

67
00:02:45,755 --> 00:02:46,879
The hard side.

68
00:02:46,879 --> 00:02:51,107
Too much directing becomes micromanaging,
and people stop thinking for

69
00:02:51,107 --> 00:02:52,007
themselves.

70
00:02:52,312 --> 00:02:55,439
And coordination gets
harder as a team grows.

71
00:02:55,789 --> 00:02:58,273
Four people have six links between them.

72
00:02:58,273 --> 00:03:00,041
Ten people have forty five.

73
00:03:00,391 --> 00:03:01,936
So the lesson is balance.

74
00:03:01,936 --> 00:03:05,059
Guide people, but trust
them, and connect them early.

75
00:03:05,709 --> 00:03:06,642
Quick check.

76
00:03:06,642 --> 00:03:10,857
Ravi gathers the team a week before
the festival, not on the day.

77
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:13,369
Which principle of coordination is this?

78
00:03:15,269 --> 00:03:16,310
Early stages!

79
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:19,965
Coordinate while plans are
made, before problems start.

80
00:03:20,565 --> 00:03:21,574
So, remember.

81
00:03:21,874 --> 00:03:26,258
Directing guides people, with
supervision, communication, leadership and

82
00:03:26,258 --> 00:03:27,158
motivation.

83
00:03:27,460 --> 00:03:31,317
Coordinating makes all the work
fit together, at the right time.

84
00:03:31,667 --> 00:03:36,178
And Follett's four: direct contact,
early stages, reciprocal relating,

85
00:03:36,178 --> 00:03:37,945
and a continuous process.

86
00:03:38,545 --> 00:03:42,318
Next time, Ravi checks whether
his plans are really working.

87
00:03:42,318 --> 00:03:43,531
That's controlling.
